  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A pure sample of nuclide X decays into nuclide Y. The graph shows how <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span>, the ratio of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Number  of  nuclides  Y}{Number  of  nuclides  of  X}\"></span> in the sample, varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The half-life of nuclide Z is four times the half-life of nuclide X. When a pure sample of nuclide Z decays, the activity of the sample after <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span> hours is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15\"></span> Bq. What is the initial activity of the pure sample of nuclide Z?  </p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30\"></span> Bq</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60\"></span> Bq</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"120\"></span> Bq</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"240\"></span> Bq</li>\n</ol>"
  },
